<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isenheim Altarpiece</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1512">1512</a>–<a href="/years/1516">1516</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Isenheim Altarpiece is a large folding altarpiece painted by Matthias Grünewald, with carvings by Nikolaus of Haguenau, for the Antonite monastery at Isenheim in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> between 1512 and 1516. Its harrowing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crucifixion">Crucifixion</a> was made for a hospital that treated sufferers of ergotism. It is now in the Unterlinden Museum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colmar">Colmar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isenheim-altarpiece.jpg" alt="Isenheim Altarpiece" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matthias Grünewald / Nikolaus Hagenauer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isenheim_Altarpiece_-_In_situ_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
